<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.10.6 Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01034</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.10.6 Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>601ca5aa-a1ce-4d96-99d7-52d07a04f44c</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>Use the following scenario and graph to answer question 1. </para>
  <blockquote>
    <para>Functions \(R\) and \(D\) give the height, in feet, of a toy rocket and a drone, \(t\) seconds after they are released.</para>
  </blockquote>    
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="68b440d2-ddaa-4395-b1ea-cf50c5776df1" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="dda9a192-afb9-4d84-af71-cf27430be6a1" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="True" data-solution-options="[&quot;True&quot;, &quot;False&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Here are the graphs of \(R\) (for the rocket) and \(D\) (for the drone).</para>
      <image alt="Two functions graphed on a cooridnate plane." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/6953fee5f8d02223583c335e6d1949b8e372de5f"/><para>Decide whether the following statements are true or false.</para>
      <para> \(R(3)&gt;D(3)\) </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! True</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="8d4965ce-4ed6-47c7-84a5-8f386fd24131" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="False" data-solution-options="[&quot;True&quot;, &quot;False&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> \(R(0)=D(0)\) </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! False</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6dfc5704-a1ba-4f7b-a75e-ca6124401256" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="True" data-solution-options="[&quot;True&quot;, &quot;False&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> \(R(4.5)=D(4.5)\) </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! True</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="806539da-ea72-4105-8022-54c376c3d87a" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="True" data-solution-options="[&quot;True&quot;, &quot;False&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> \(R(0)=D(0)+25\) </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! True</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1e-->
  <exercise data-content-id="1d35db9a-6af8-44ae-bec5-d9bb9b0cfad3" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="False" data-solution-options="[&quot;True&quot;, &quot;False&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(D(7)&gt;R(5)\) </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! False</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0ddaab9d-60de-4e61-a407-65e98a20f548" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="Minneapolis" data-solution-options="[&quot;Aspen&quot;, &quot;Minneapolis&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(A(t)\) is the average high temperature in Aspen, Colorado, \(t\) months after the start of the year. \(M(t)\) is the average high temperature in Minneapolis, Minnesota, \(t\) months after the start of the year. Temperature is measured in degrees Fahrenheit.</para><image alt="" class="img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom" height="278" role="presentation" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/7b3766d3ead874b4e2db8f1013d3f0b5420120a9" width="300"/><para>Which function had the higher average rate of change between the beginning of January and middle of March?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Minneapolis</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.10.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="9a273719-f18c-482a-b3ba-fe24ef89a14f" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;There are values of \\(x\\) where \\(f(x)=g(x)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(-1)\\) &lt; \\(g(-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(-3)\\) &gt; \\(g(4)\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(f(0)\\) &gt; \\(g(0)\\)&quot;, &quot;There are values of \\(x\\) where \\(f(x)=g(x)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(-1)\\) &lt; \\(g(-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(-3)\\) &gt; \\(g(4)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Here are two graphs representing functions \(f\) and \(g\). <image src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/30220e31ee1b23d05fb738dae100f8116e999253"/><emphasis>Select the three </emphasis>statements that are true about functions \(f\) and \(g\). </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! There are values of \(x\) where \(f(x)=g(x)\), \(f(-1)&lt;g(-1)\), and \(f(-3)&gt;g(4)\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="4e794bf6-e260-4a61-a58a-17ac911bdea1" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="Runner C" data-solution-options="[&quot;Runner A&quot;, &quot;Runner B&quot;, &quot;Runner C&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For questions 4–6, use the three graphs below:</para>
      <blockquote>
        <para>The three graphs represent the progress of three runners in a 400-meter race.</para>
      </blockquote>
      <image src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/c921ccce5023a038cae710698ab652dcf8a30c16"/><para>Which runner ran at a constant rate throughout the race?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Runner C</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.10.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="04ab420e-4add-46e5-882c-2d284935828d" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="Runner A" data-solution-options="[&quot;Runner A&quot;, &quot;Runner B&quot;, &quot;Runner C&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which runner stopped running for a while?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Runner A</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.10.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f6688a12-f180-460e-adbe-77007465867b" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="Runner C" data-solution-options="[&quot;Runner A&quot;, &quot;Runner B&quot;, &quot;Runner C&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which runner won the race?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Runner C</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.10.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6051a616-ba9f-4e8b-9a5f-e1609189532b" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="Show B" data-solution-options="[&quot;Show A&quot;, &quot;Show B&quot;, &quot;Show C&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Use the graphs below for questions 7–8.</para>
      <para>Show A                                             Show B                                   Show C</para>
      <image src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4ac31af5cda20f893e4a37940e125dea4f2d0f23" width="550"/><para>Which show had the largest audience for episode 4?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Show B</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="59eb0e33-4424-4a1b-8eae-2ef7a75ce41c" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="Show B" data-solution-options="[&quot;Show A&quot;, &quot;Show B&quot;, &quot;Show C&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which show had the largest audience for their first episode?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Show B</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.10.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div></section>
